{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat run_trace/galaxy_tool_run_003/request.json; echo '--- validation'; cat run_trace/galaxy_tool_run_003/validation_response.json | head -200\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b51c17a7800f17d8aa\",\n  \"input_format\": \"auto\",\n  \"selected_input_format\": \"21.01\",\n  \"tool_id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/bgruening/text_processing/tp_sort_header_tool/9.5+galaxy3\",\n  \"tool_inputs\": {\n    \"header\": 0,\n    \"infile\": {\n      \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721350a0311157466a093\",\n      \"src\": \"hda\"\n    },\n    \"sortkeys\": [\n      {\n        \"column\": \"c5\",\n        \"ignore_case\": false,\n        \"ignore_leading_blanks\": false,\n        \"order\": \"r\",\n        \"style\": \"n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"unique\": false\n  },\n  \"validate_before_submit\": true\n}\n--- validation\n{\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Organization\",\n      \"name\": \"European Galaxy Team\",\n      \"url\": \"https://galaxyproject.org/eu/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gr\\u00fcning\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Bj\\u00f6rn\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bgruening\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gordon\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Assaf\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/agordon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Bernt\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Matthias\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bernt-matthias/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"data in ascending or descending order\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<p><strong>What it does</strong></p>\\n<p>This tool sorts an input file.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Sorting Styles</strong></p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>Fast Numeric</strong>: sort by numeric values. Handles integer values (e.g. 43, 134) and decimal-point values (e.g. 3.14). <em>Does not</em> handle scientific notation (e.g. -2.32e2).</li>\\n<li><strong>General Numeric</strong>: sort by numeric values. Handles all numeric notations (including scientific notation). Slower than <em>fast numeric</em>, so use only when necessary.</li>\\n<li><strong>Natural Sort</strong>: Sort in 'natural' order (natural to humans, not to computers). See example below.</li>\\n<li><strong>Alphabetical sort</strong>: Sort in strict alphabetical order. See example below.</li>\\n<li><strong>Human-readable numbers</strong>: Sort human readble numbers (e.g. 1G &gt; 2M &gt; 3K &gt; 400)</li>\\n<li><strong>Random order</strong>: return lines in random order.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example - Header line</strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Input file</strong> (note first line is a header line, should not be sorted):</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nFruit   Color   Price\\nBanana  Yellow  4.1\\nAvocado Green   8.0\\nApple   Red     3.0\\nMelon   Green   6.1\\n</pre>\\n<p><strong>Sorting</strong> by <strong>numeric order</strong> on column <strong>3</strong>, with <strong>header</strong>, will return:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nFruit   Color   Price\\nApple   Red     3.0\\nBanana  Yellow  4.1\\nMelon   Green   6.1\\nAvocado Green   8.0\\n</pre>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example - Natural vs. Alphabetical sorting</strong></p>\\n<p>Given the following list:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nchr4\\nchr13\\nchr1\\nchr10\\nchr20\\nchr2\\n</pre>\\n<p><strong>Alphabetical sort</strong> would produce the following sorted list:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nchr1\\nchr10\\nchr13\\nchr2\\nchr20\\nchr4\\n</pre>\\n<p><strong>Natural Sort</strong> would produce the following sorted list:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nchr1\\nchr2\\nchr4\\nchr10\\nchr13\\nchr20\\n</pre>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\">If you're planning to use the file with another tool that expected sorted files (such as <em>join</em>), you should use the <strong>Alphabetical sort</strong>,  not the <strong>Natural Sort</strong>. Natural sort order is easier for humans, but is unnatural for computer programs.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example - Sorting based on parts of column values</strong></p>\\n<p>The above column of chromosomes, with their constant prefix, could have been sorted in natural order also with the <strong>Fast numeric sort</strong> and <strong>considering its characters from</strong> character 4 only.</p>\\n<p>In general, sorting based on just a range of characters in a column can be useful for sorting values with internal structure, in a single tool run.</p>\\n<p>Consider, for example, the following column of dates, which is unfortunately not ISO-8601 formatted:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\n10/24/2025\\n09/18/1974\\n12/16/1998\\n03/04/2007\\n</pre>\\n<p>You could modify these values with other tools first, but you can achieve correct chronological sort order with a single run of the sort tool like this:</p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li>Do a <strong>Fast numeric sort</strong> on the column <strong>considering its characters from</strong> character 7 (the start of the year).</li>\\n<li>Resolve ties (using another column selection section) with another <strong>Fast numeric sort</strong> on the same column <strong>considering its characters from</strong> character 1 <strong>to and including</strong> character 2 (the month representation).</li>\\n<li>Resolve remaining ties with a third <strong>Fast numeric sort</strong> on again the same column <strong>considering its characters from</strong> character 4 <strong>to and including</strong> character 5 (the day representation).</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>This will result in the ascending chronological order:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\n09/18/1974\\n11/17/1998\\n11/18/1998\\n12/16/1998\\n03/04/2007\\n10/24/2025\\n</pre>\\n<p>Before relying on in-column character ranges, make extra sure that all values are formatted consistently (in the above example, that all dates use two digits for days and months and the same overall date format).</p>\\n\",\n  \"help_format\": \"restructuredtext\",\n  \"hidden\": \"\",\n  \"hidden_versions\": [],\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b51c17a7800f17d8aa\",\n  \"icon\": null,\n  \"id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/bgruening/text_processing/tp_sort_header_tool/9.5+galaxy3\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"argument\": null,\n      \"default_value\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721350a0311157466a093\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"edam\": {\n        \"edam_data\": [\n          \"data_0006\"\n        ],\n        \"edam_formats\": [\n          \"format_3475\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"extensions\": [\n        \"tabular\"\n      ],\n      \"help\": \"\",\n      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n      \"hidden\": false,\n      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n      \"label\": \"Sort Query\",\n      \"model_class\": \"DataToolParameter\",\n      \"multiple\": false,\n      \"name\": \"infile\",\n      \"optional\": false,\n      \"options\": {\n        \"dce\": [],\n        \"hda\": [\n          {\n            \"hid\": 91,\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721350a0311157466a093\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"Filter on dataset 90\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\",\n            \"tags\": []\n          }\n        ],\n        \"hdca\": [\n          {\n            \"hid\": 89,\n            \"id\": \"0c09e3503f4dd63c\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"Excel to Tabular on dataset 2\",\n            \"src\": \"hdca\",\n            \"tags\": []\n          }\n        ],\n        \"ldda\": []\n      },\n      \"options_meta\": {\n        \"hda\": {\n          \"has_more\": false,\n          \"limit\": 50,\n          \"offset\": 0,\n          \"total_estimate\": 1\n        },\n        \"hdca\": {\n          \"has_more\": false,\n          \"limit\": 50,\n          \"offset\": 0,\n          \"total_estimate\": 1\n        }\n      },\n      \"pinned\": {\n        \"dce\": [],\n        \"hda\": [],\n        \"hdca\": [],\n        \"ldda\": []\n      },\n      \"refresh_on_change\": true,\n      \"tag\": null,\n      \"text_value\": \"No dataset.\",\n      \"type\": \"data\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721350a0311157466a093\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"area\": false,\n      \"argument\": null,\n      \"datalist\": [],\n      \"default_value\": \"0\",\n      \"help\": \"Header lines will be copied to the output unchanged without operating on them.\",\n      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n      \"hidden\": false,\n      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n      \"label\": \"Number of header lines\",\n      \"max\": null,\n      \"min\": null,\n      \"model_class\": \"IntegerToolParameter\",\n      \"name\": \"header\",\n      \"optional\": false,\n      \"refresh_on_change\": false,\n      \"text_value\": \"0\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"value\": \"0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cache\": [\n        [\n          {\n            \"argument\": null,\n            \"data_ref\": \"infile\",\n            \"default_value\": null,\n            \"display\": null,\n            \"help\": \"\",\n            \"help_format\": \"html\",\n            \"hidden\": false,\n            \"is_dynamic\": true,\n            \"label\": \"Sort on column\",\n            \"model_class\": \"ColumnListParameter\",\n            \"multiple\": false,\n            \"name\": \"column\",\